1
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:12,000
Message from the King is a action, mystery, thriller
film directed by Fabrice Du Welz.

2
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:18,000
On a relentless quest to avenge his sister's murder, a man from Cape Town
infiltrates a sprawling network of lowlifes and elites in Los Angeles.

3
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:24,000
Jacob King, played by Chadwick Boseman.

4
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:30,000
Wentworth, played by Luke Evans.

5
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
Preston, played by Alfred Molina.

6
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:42,000
Kelly, played by Teresa Palmer.

7
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Trish, played by Natalie Martinez.

8
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:54,000
Leary, played by Chris Mulkey.

9
00:45:54,000 --> 00:46:00,000
Message from the King is a 2016 revenge-action-thriller film directed by
Fabrice Du Welz, and written by Stephen Cornwell and Oliver Butcher.

10
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
The film is produced by Cornwell, David Lancaster and Simon Cornwell and stars
Chadwick Boseman, Luke Evans, Teresa Palmer, and Alfred Molina.

11
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:12,000
The film's plot revolves around Jacob King (Boseman), a man from Cape Town, South Africa who travels to Los Angeles
in order to find his younger sister and, after finding out she is dead, he works to avenge her death.

12
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
The project was announced on November 4, 2014, along with Boseman's casting.

13
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:24,000
Principal photography began in February 2015 in Los Angeles, California.

14
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
Other filming locations included Cape Town, South
Africa, Glendale, Beverly Hills and Topanga.

15
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The film premiered at the 2016 Toronto International
Film Festival on September 8, 2016.

16
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:42,000
It received mixed reviews from critics, with praise directed at Boseman's
performance and criticism aimed at the script and the overall pacing.

17
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:48,000
Netflix released the film on August 4, 2017.

18
01:31:48,000 --> 01:31:54,000
The film explores themes of tattoo, morgue,
flashback, money, los angeles, california.

19
01:36:54,000 --> 01:37:00,000
The tone is intense and mind_bending.
